 ],
 "synopsis": "J Infratech Ltd has filed draft papers with SEBI for an initial public offering consisting of a fresh issue of shares worth ₹600 crore and an offer for sale of one crore equity shares by its promoters. The Haryana-based road and bridge builder may also raise up to ₹120 crore through a pre-IPO placement, which would correspondingly reduce the fresh issue size. Proceeds from the newly issued shares will be used by the company for working capital and debt repayment, while proceeds from the offer for sale will go to the promoters selling their holdings. Systematix Corporate Services is acting as the book-running lead manager, and KFin Technologies is the registrar.",
